      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Securing a minor burn with a barrier is excellent advice, but your injury has already progressed to the degree that blisters are forming, which requires sterile care beyond just applying cream. Most minor first-degree burns (just red skin without blisters) do heal well at home, but you should avoid creating your own sterile environment at home due to the high risk of infection from greasy substances. I highly recommend calling a nurse advice line or your doctor's office for a quick, usually lower-cost consultation to confirm if your specific case can be managed safely at home without unnecessary complications.",
